*.js text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.go text eol=lf
# A GOLDEN IS COMPARED BYTE FOR BYTE, so its line endings are part of the artifact. Without
# these two, a Windows checkout converts them to CRLF while the code that derives them emits LF,
# and the file differs from itself on one platform — `the derived schema differs from
# testdata/schema.sql` with no change to the schema. Same reason the five above are pinned.
*.sql text eol=lf
*.golden text eol=lf
